From 51b3940ddb801d9b5fdcc033bbf332c7d2861e4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:15:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): Sodick wire skim passes state their flushing

A wire machine file can state edm.skim_flushing (high / low), the
flushing of each skim pass. The Sodick wire post writes its T word
(T84 / T85) before each skim's C word. The rough cut keeps
edm.flushing, written after each threading (#1499).

edm.skim_flushing needs edm.flushing: the T word is modal, so a skim's
flushing would stay active for the next rough cut. The machine file
parser, Edm::is_sane, Edm::refusal and the post refuse a file that
states only the skim flushing.

A skim on a machine that states edm.flushing and no edm.skim_flushing
is refused by name: the skim's flushing is not known, and the post does
not cut it on the rough cut's flushing. A machine that states no
flushing posts its skims as before (#2649).

The machine editor offers the choice while a flushing is stated. The
MCP edit_machine tool takes the key through the same machine patch.
The generic ISO wire post notes a stated skim flushing that it does not
program.

Decision: docs/decisions/2686-sodick-skim-flushing.md

Fixes #2686

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
